-This family of methods modifies the appearance or geometry of a scene represented by a neural radiance field $F_\Theta$ to remove unwanted objects, insert new content, or alter semantic regions. It solves the problem of localized scene alteration while preserving multi-view consistency and the integrity of unedited regions. Unlike standard training loops that optimize weights from scratch, these procedures either intercept the volume rendering process at inference time (zero-shot, non-iterative) or perform targeted optimization of existing parameters using auxiliary guidance (e.g., 2D inpainting priors, diffusion models, or semantic features).
